{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicEnergy.actual_macroscopic_gradient_energy_blocks",
      "title": "Actual macroscopic reflection blocks and sharp smooth gradient energy",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.E2",
          "label": "Fixed PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 B.1-B.9 actual conditional projection/reflection compression and variance defect; C.1 formula(C.2) smooth compact energy. B.13 rough-domain and B.10-B.11 Gamma excluded.",
          "scope": "Actual joint L2 block and smooth compact energy integration, SAME law/kernels/operators and classical integral representative; actual variance equals microscopic block norm-square. Full rough L2-H1/outer closed-gradient/Gamma/half-turn/main/implementation error/expected costs/composition remain separate. Focused build passed3891; independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSMacroscopicEnergy"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert space E with Borel structure; rank zero is an explicit authored extension of the source Euclidean setting.",
        "Globally C² potential V; 0<α≤β and the genuine pointwise Hessian bounds α‖a‖²≤D²V(x)[a,a]≤β‖a‖².",
        "Positive step η with βη≤1, exactly the source restriction.",
        "Signed smooth compactly supported f. All probabilities, kernels, L² classes, differentiability, L²/L¹ domains and block/variance identities are produced internally."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, including rank zero. Let V be globally C² and 0<α≤β, with α‖a‖²≤D²V(x)[a,a]≤β‖a‖² for every x,a. Suppose η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ as the normalized volume tilt exp(-V), J as the actual law of (X,X+√η G) for independent X∼μ and standard Gaussian G, ν=J.snd, Λ as the law of (Y,2X-Y), and F(x,y)=(x,2x-y). The theorem produces probability of μ,J,ν and common Markov kernels R,S, with swapped J disintegrated by R, every-y reflected S, its exact normalized density, and Λ=ν⊗S. On the actual Hilbert space L²(J), P is conditional projection given Y; one common U is the genuine reflection pullback, a self-adjoint isometric involution. With authored aliases A=PUP, B=(I-P)UP and D=(I-P)U(I-P), B*B=P-A² and B*D=-AB*. For every Pg=g, ‖Bg‖²=‖g‖²-‖Ag‖². For each signed smooth compactly supported f, the literal Tf(y)=∫f(u)S_y(du) is differentiable, f,Tf,∇Tf lie in L²(ν), and Var_Sf lies in L¹(ν). A genuine class g=[f∘snd] satisfies Pg=g and Ag=[Tf∘snd]; its actual squared norm and the squared norm of Ag equal ∫f²dν and ∫(Tf)²dν. Moreover ∫Var_Sf dν=‖Bg‖² and η∫‖∇Tf‖²dν≤(1-αη)²/[4(1+αη)]‖Bg‖². No centering or law, operator, representative, domain or bound certificate is a public assumption.",
      "formula": "\\int\\operatorname{Var}_{S_y}(f)\\,\\nu(dy)=\\|Bg\\|_{L^2(J)}^2=\\|g\\|_{L^2(J)}^2-\\|Ag\\|_{L^2(J)}^2,\\qquad\\eta\\int\\|\\nabla Tf\\|^2\\,d\\nu\\le\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\|Bg\\|_{L^2(J)}^2.",
      "boundary": "Actual joint L2 block and smooth compact energy integration, SAME law/kernels/operators and classical integral representative; actual variance equals microscopic block norm-square. Full rough L2-H1/outer closed-gradient/Gamma/half-turn/main/implementation error/expected costs/composition remain separate. Focused build passed3891; independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Keep one genuine conditional kernel and literal smooth mean",
          "text": "Reuse the genuine outer-energy producer to obtain μ,J,ν as probabilities and one common R,S before choosing f. The same S gives every-y reflection and normalized density. Its literal integral Tf already has genuine differentiability and all finite domains; these outputs stay attached to this S throughout.",
          "formula": "Tf(y)=\\int f(u)S_y(du),\\quad S_y=(x\\mapsto2x-y)_\\#R_y,\\quad\\nabla Tf\\in L^2(\\nu).",
          "lean": "ConditionalGradientEnergy.reflected_conditional_gradient_energy; henergy; hcond; hSR; hSd"
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce the actual reflected-pair disintegration",
          "text": "Map the actual swapped-joint disintegration through (y,x)↦(y,2x-y). Measurability and the exact setwise kernel-map formula show that the resulting measure is ν⊗S and is precisely Λ. Its first coordinate is the actual ν; this is a derived law identity, not a caller premise.",
          "formula": "\\Lambda=(y,2x-y)_\\#(\\nu\\otimes R)=\\nu\\otimes S,\\qquad\\Lambda_\\mathrm{fst}=\\nu.",
          "lean": "hG; hmap; hΛmap; hfst; hΛcond; Measure.compProd_apply; Measure.map_apply; Measure.disintegrate"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use AE uniqueness only for conditional means and classes",
          "text": "The macroscopic representative parent has a kernel S₀ disintegrating the same Λ. Genuine conditional-kernel uniqueness gives S=S₀ almost everywhere under ν. Lift this equality along snd to J. It identifies integral values and L² representatives; it does not transport pointwise derivatives. We retain the original differentiable Tf from the first step.",
          "formula": "S=S_0\\quad\\nu\\text{-a.e.},\\qquad Tf(Y)=T_0f(Y)\\quad J\\text{-a.e.}.",
          "lean": "eq_condKernel_of_measure_eq_compProd; hκ; ae_of_ae_map; hκJ; hAgS"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the actual reflection operators and retain block algebra",
          "text": "Both producer isometries act on the same L²(J) by composition with F. Their AE actions agree, hence Lp extensionality identifies the isometries. This joins the actual macroscopic representative with the genuine reflection block identities, using the actual comap-snd projection P.",
          "formula": "U_0=U,\\quad A=PUP,\\quad B=(I-P)UP,\\quad D=(I-P)U(I-P),\\quad B^*B=P-A^2,\\quad B^*D=-AB^*.",
          "lean": "MacroscopicRepresentative.macroscopic_reflection_smooth_representative; ReflectionL2.actual_reflection_block_identities; LinearIsometry.ext; Lp.ext; hUU; hBB; hBD; hblock"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify both actual second moments",
          "text": "The real Hilbert inner product expresses each squared L² norm as the integral of its representative squared. Use the actual AE representatives and ν=J.snd to transport the two moments. Continuity of f and of the genuine Tf supplies the measurable integral-map domain. No hypothetical squared-norm identity is assumed.",
          "formula": "g=[f\\circ\\mathrm{snd}],\\quad Ag=[Tf\\circ\\mathrm{snd}],\\quad\\|g\\|^2=\\int f^2d\\nu,\\quad\\|Ag\\|^2=\\int(Tf)^2d\\nu.",
          "lean": "norm_snd (fixed actual J/ν local adapter, twice consumed); L2.inner_def; real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq; integral_congr_ae; integral_map; hgn; hAgn"
        },
        {
          "title": "Close the genuine microscopic variance identity",
          "text": "The outer-energy producer gives the exact integrated conditional variance defect. Substitute the two genuine second moments and the actual reflection-block norm defect for Pg=g. The same S therefore supplies the microscopic block norm-square.",
          "formula": "\\int\\operatorname{Var}_{S_y}(f)d\\nu=\\int f^2d\\nu-\\int(Tf)^2d\\nu=\\|g\\|^2-\\|Ag\\|^2=\\|Bg\\|^2.",
          "lean": "hvar; hgn; hAgn; hblock g hPg; hvariance"
        },
        {
          "title": "Join the exact smooth gradient bound",
          "text": "Substitute the genuine variance/block identity into the already proved sharp smooth energy estimate. Every domain and the actual Bg are now internal outputs. This is the smooth compact block input used toward B.13; it does not construct Γ or extend the gradient operator to arbitrary rough L² classes.",
          "formula": "\\eta\\int\\|\\nabla Tf\\|^2d\\nu\\le\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\left(\\int f^2d\\nu-\\int(Tf)^2d\\nu\\right)=\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\|Bg\\|^2.",
          "lean": "hbound; hvar; hvariance"
        },
        {
          "title": "Exercise zero energy and a noncentered class",
          "text": "At V=‖x‖²/2 and α=β=η=1, the sharp coefficient is zero and the actual smooth gradient energy vanishes. In rank zero the constant f=1 is smooth with compact support: its genuine class has norm-square one, Ag=g, and microscopic block/conditional variance/gradient energy zero. This verifies that no hidden centering premise entered the class or norm bridge.",
          "formula": "\\alpha=\\beta=\\eta=1\\Rightarrow\\int\\|\\nabla Tf\\|^2d\\nu=0;\\qquad d=0,\\ f=1\\Rightarrow\\|g\\|^2=1,\\ Ag=g,\\ \\|Bg\\|^2=0.",
          "lean": "Tests.ProximalBPSMacroscopicEnergy.gaussian_precision_macroscopic_energy; rank_zero_noncentered_constant"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, including rank zero. Let V be globally C² and 0<α≤β, with α‖a‖²≤D²V(x)[a,a]≤β‖a‖² for every x,a. Suppose η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ as the normalized volume tilt exp(-V), J as the actual law of (X,X+√η G) for independent X∼μ and standard Gaussian G, ν=J.snd, Λ as the law of (Y,2X-Y), and F(x,y)=(x,2x-y). The theorem produces probability of μ,J,ν and common Markov kernels R,S, with swapped J disintegrated by R, every-y reflected S, its exact normalized density, and Λ=ν⊗S. On the actual Hilbert space L²(J), P is conditional projection given Y; one common U is the genuine reflection pullback, a self-adjoint isometric involution. With authored aliases A=PUP, B=(I-P)UP and D=(I-P)U(I-P), B*B=P-A² and B*D=-AB*. For every Pg=g, ‖Bg‖²=‖g‖²-‖Ag‖². For each signed smooth compactly supported f, the literal Tf(y)=∫f(u)S_y(du) is differentiable, f,Tf,∇Tf lie in L²(ν), and Var_Sf lies in L¹(ν). A genuine class g=[f∘snd] satisfies Pg=g and Ag=[Tf∘snd]; its actual squared norm and the squared norm of Ag equal ∫f²dν and ∫(Tf)²dν. Moreover ∫Var_Sf dν=‖Bg‖² and η∫‖∇Tf‖²dν≤(1-αη)²/[4(1+αη)]‖Bg‖². No centering or law, operator, representative, domain or bound certificate is a public assumption.",
      "lean_proof": "Keep one genuine conditional kernel and literal smooth mean; Produce the actual reflected-pair disintegration; Use AE uniqueness only for conditional means and classes; Identify the actual reflection operators and retain block algebra; Identify both actual second moments; Close the genuine microscopic variance identity; Join the exact smooth gradient bound; Exercise zero energy and a noncentered class",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalGradientEnergy.reflected_conditional_gradient_energy",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicRepresentative.macroscopic_reflection_smooth_representative",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ReflectionL2.actual_reflection_block_identities",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.variance"
      ],
      "mathlib_dependencies": [
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.compProd_apply",
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.map_apply",
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.map_map",
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.fst_map_prodMk",
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.fst_map_swap",
        "MeasureTheory.Measure.disintegrate",
        "ProbabilityTheory.eq_condKernel_of_measure_eq_compProd",
        "MeasureTheory.ae_of_ae_map",
        "LinearIsometry.ext",
        "MeasureTheory.Lp.ext",
        "MeasureTheory.L2.inner_def",
        "real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq",
        "MeasureTheory.integral_congr_ae",
        "MeasureTheory.integral_map"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
